# Sandbox environment reference (Claude Code cloud, Codex cloud, or any headless
# agent sandbox). Two sections:
#
#   1. Already automatic -- scripts/cloud-env-setup.sh generates every one of
#      these itself when it runs. Nothing to do; listed here so you know what
#      exists and isn't missing.
#   2. You must configure these yourself -- as environment variables in your
#      agent platform's cloud environment settings (e.g. Codex's "Environment
#      variables" panel, Claude Code cloud's environment config), not in this
#      file. The setup script cannot generate them because they're real
#      third-party credentials.
#
# Forge has three modes: mainnet, testnet, preview (this sandbox's disposable
# Anvil chain). The backend has two: development, production. The web app and
# facilitator each have one mode -- just configuration, no network-switching
# logic of their own.

# =============================================================================
# 1. ALREADY AUTOMATIC -- generated by scripts/cloud-env-setup.sh
# =============================================================================
#
# Backend (apps/backend/src/config/env.ts): NODE_ENV, PORT, DATABASE_URL,
#   CHAIN_ID, BASE_RPC_URL, CONTRACT_ADDRESS, FORWARDER_ADDRESS,
#   USDC_TOKEN_ADDRESS, DEFAULT_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS, USDC_DOMAIN_NAME,
#   CORS_ORIGIN, SERVER_PRIVATE_KEY, PLATFORM_MASTER_KEY (freshly random per
#   sandbox), X402_FACILITATOR_URL, ERC8004_IDENTITY_REGISTRY,
#   ERC8004_REPUTATION_REGISTRY, ERC8004_SEED_BLOCK, SUBMISSION_FREE_ALLOWANCE
#   (raised to 1000 in this sandbox -- RFC-0006 Tier 1, so the smoke suite's
#   ordinary multi-submission coverage never needs x402Post just to keep
#   submitting; production default is 3).
#
# Contract deploy scripts (packages/contracts/script/*.s.sol), every one
#   suffixed _PREVIEW to match `make deploy preview`: FORGE_RPC_URL_PREVIEW,
#   FORGE_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY_PREVIEW, FORGE_FEE_RECIPIENT_ADDRESS_PREVIEW,
#   FORGE_DEFAULT_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS_PREVIEW, FORGE_SERVER_ADDRESS_PREVIEW, plus
#   this run's deploy outputs: FORGE_USDC_TOKEN_ADDRESS_PREVIEW,
#   FORGE_DIAMOND_ADDRESS_PREVIEW, FORGE_FORWARDER_ADDRESS_PREVIEW.
#
# Smoke tests (apps/backend/scripts/smoke-*.ts) -- every role its own
#   dedicated Anvil account: DEV_PRIVATE_KEY, REQUESTER_PRIVATE_KEY,
#   WORKER_PRIVATE_KEY, WORKER_B_PRIVATE_KEY, EVALUATOR_PRIVATE_KEY.
#
# CLI (apps/cli/src/lib/api.ts): TASKMARKET_API_URL, pointed at this
#   sandbox's own backend. Build + run with `make cli <args>`.
#
# Facilitator (started locally, cloned from the public daydreamsai/facilitator
#   repo -- no credentials needed): PORT, EVM_NETWORKS, EVM_RPC_URL_BASE_SEPOLIA,
#   EVM_PRIVATE_KEY, TRACKING_ALLOW_IN_MEMORY_FALLBACK.
#
# Web app (apps/web, NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix): NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,
#   TASKMARKET_API_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS, NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID,
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL.

# =============================================================================
# 2. YOU MUST SET THESE -- in your agent platform's environment configuration,
#    not in this file. Only needed if the task actually touches the feature.
# =============================================================================

# Email-worker (apps/email-worker) sending real email via Resend. Get from
# your own Resend account or another developer. Not needed unless testing
# outbound email delivery -- agent-to-agent routing works via direct DB
# insert with no config at all.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Web app auth / embedded wallets (Privy). Get from the team's Privy
# dashboard or another developer. Not needed unless testing the web app's
# auth/wallet flows.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=
